From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:51:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: apple,prores: Name the T8132
 initialization table

T8132 takes a per-machine initialization table like T6041 and T6050.
Name it in the description.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,prores.yaml | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,prores.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,prores.yaml
index 69be59afd4..6e7bbcfc73 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,prores.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,prores.yaml
@@ -12,9 +12,10 @@ maintainers:
 description: |
   The APR is a directly programmed ProRes engine with its own DART. Jobs are
   descriptors in a DMA ring; the engine signals completion with an
-  interrupt. On T6041 and T6050 a per-machine initialization table,
-  apple/prores-t6041-init.bin or apple/prores-t6050-init.bin, takes the
-  place of any rows built into the driver. Other supported variants have no
+  interrupt. On T8132, T6041 and T6050 a per-machine initialization table,
+  apple/prores-t8132-init.bin, apple/prores-t6041-init.bin or
+  apple/prores-t6050-init.bin, takes the place of any rows built into the
+  driver. Other supported variants have no
   firmware.
   The engine's power domain also resets it.
 
-- 
